        qudt:Unit ;
    rdfs:label "Coulomb per Cubic Metre"@en,
        "Coulomb per Cubic Meter"@en-US ;
    dct:description "Coulomb Per Cubic Meter ($C/m^{3}$) is a unit in the category of Electric charge density. It is also known as coulomb per cubic metre, coulombs per cubic meter, coulombs per cubic metre, coulomb/cubic meter, coulomb/cubic metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Coulomb Per Cubic Meter has a dimension of $L^{-3}TI$ where $L$ is length, $T$ is time, and $I$ is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category."^^qudt:LatexString ;
