    dct:description """Metre per second is an SI derived unit of both speed (scalar) and velocity (vector quantity which specifies both magnitude and a specific direction), defined by distance in metres divided by time in seconds.
The official SI symbolic abbreviation is mu00b7s-1, or equivalently either m/s."""^^rdf:HTML ;
